{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJMComm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeStableScalarCascade"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw_roundTrip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw_roundTrip","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L202-L210","doc":"**The round trip.**  Rescaling `σ ↦ q·σ` into Iwahori normalisation and back through the bridge\nreturns `σ`.  This is what would break if the scaling were inverted, or if the bridge used `Q = q`\nrather than `Q = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw_isHeckeGeneratorsBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw_isHeckeGeneratorsBelow","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L184-L200","doc":"They satisfy the Iwahori relations at `Q = q²`, so `heckeGeneratorsBelow_of_iwahori` applies —\nthe bridge has a concrete `dim = 2` input, not merely a hypothesised one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoIw","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L178-L182","doc":"The explicit `2×2` seminormal generators in **Iwahori** normalisation: `T i = q · σ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.iwahori_of_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.iwahori_of_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L159-L174","doc":"**The inverse rescaling.**  If `S` satisfies the corpus relation at `q`, then `q·S` satisfies\nthe Iwahori relation at `Q = q²`.\n\nNo `q ≠ 0` needed, unlike `hecke_of_iwahori`: this direction multiplies by `q` rather than by\n`q⁻¹`, and the identity survives `q = 0` (where Lean's `q⁻¹ = 0` makes both sides collapse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.iwahori_jm_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.iwahori_jm_comm","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L126-L141","doc":"**The payoff, demonstrated.**  An Iwahori-normalised family at `Q = q²` inherits Jucys–Murphy\ncommutativity with no further hypotheses — the arc's theorems reach it through the bridge.\n\n`jmRawB_comm` is the arc's result; everything this needed from the Iwahori side is the three\nrelations at `Q = q²`.  The same composition carries `jmProdB_eq_deltaPowB`, `IsJMWeightB` and the\ntheta tie-in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.heckeGeneratorsBelow_of_iwahori","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.heckeGeneratorsBelow_of_iwahori","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L114-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.far_of_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.far_of_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L99-L103","doc":"**Far commutation is scale-invariant** — degree 2 on both sides, so `c²` cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.braid_of_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.braid_of_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L93-L97","doc":"**Braid is scale-invariant** — degree 3 on both sides, so `c³` cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_of_iwahori_algebraMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_of_iwahori_algebraMap","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L83-L91","doc":"The same statement in `algebraMap` form — the shape `HeckeGeneratorsBelow.hecke` expects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_of_iwahori","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_of_iwahori","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeIwahoriConventionBridge.lean#L53-L81","doc":"**The quadratic bridge.**  If `T` satisfies the Iwahori relation at `Q = q²`, then `q⁻¹ · T`\nsatisfies the corpus relation at `q`.  No square root, no base-ring extension: `q ≠ 0` suffices.\n\nStated with the scalar action `•` rather than `algebraMap … * …`: the two agree by\n`Algebra.smul_def` (see `hecke_of_iwahori_algebraMap`), and `•` is what `smul_smul` /\n`smul_mul_assoc` / `mul_smul_comm` are stated for, so the scalars move without fighting\n`algebraMap`'s centrality. ","signatureChunk":0}]}